# Prefer design tokens

Use CSS custom properties from [`client/src/styles/_tokens.scss`](client/src/styles/_tokens.scss) for colors, borders, and surfaces. Theme differences belong in tokens, not scattered component overrides.

## Surfaces and borders

```scss
// ❌ BAD
border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);

[data-theme='dark'] .my-panel {
  border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
}

// ✅ GOOD
border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
background: var(--surface-hover);
```

| Need | Token |
|------|-------|
| Default border | `--border-default` |
| Divider / inner border | `--border-subtle` |
| Soft tile border | `--border-faint` |
| Hover fill | `--surface-hover` |
| Option/tile background | `--surface-interactive` |
| Card/panel background | `--surface-card` |
| Status colors | `--status-*`, `--status-*-bg`, `--status-*-border` |

## Cards and panels

- Use shared classes: `.u-glass-panel`, `.u-card`, `.card` (all flat token-based surfaces).
- **No** `box-shadow` on cards/panels.
- **No** `backdrop-filter` on cards/panels.
- **No** pseudo-element inset borders for fake depth.

Elevation shadows are allowed only for overlays: dialogs, toasts, dropdowns, focus rings.

## When hardcoded values are OK

- Brand/provider logos (Vercel black, Railway purple, etc.).
- Button gradients and glows in button components **for the default style only**.
- Terminal/log panel styling.
- Decorative animations (shimmer gradients).
- Notebook theme preview thumbnails in Settings → Appearance.

## Visual styles (`data-style`)

New visual styles (e.g. `notebook`) must be token-driven via `[data-style='…']` blocks in [`client/src/styles/_tokens.scss`](client/src/styles/_tokens.scss) or [`client/src/styles/_notebook.scss`](client/src/styles/_notebook.scss). Do not add one-off component theme branches unless a global selector cannot reach the element.

Paper shadows on cards are allowed **only** when `data-style="notebook"`.

## When editing existing code

Replace `rgba(255, 255, 255, …)` and redundant `[data-theme='dark']` blocks with tokens in the same change when you touch that file.
